  "text": "Beneath the lamps’ ethereal, pale light,\nHe walked the streets, a solitary sight.\nEach step echoed on the pavement’s stone,\nWhile ghosts of people passed, alone.\n\nTheir faces buried in worlds unseen,\nNo glance was cast, no word was spoken.\nAmid the urban sea’s cold flow,\nHe felt the weight of solitude’s blow.\n\nThe giraffe, with neck so tall and long,\nIs known for reaching where others don’t."
